### J6.5 — Request collection
### VS Code (REST Client / Humao extension), JetBrains Rider and Visual Studio 2022+ run this file directly.
### Start the app first (watch its console while you send the requests):
###   cd WebApp
###   dotnet run -- J6.5                                   (Production: Warning default, Information for this topic)
###   dotnet run -- J6.5 --environment Development         (Debug default)
###   dotnet run -- J6.5 --json                            (one JSON object per line)
###   dotnet run -- J6.5 --Logging:LogLevel:Junior.AspNetCoreFundamentals.LoggingBasics=Trace

@host = http://localhost:5080

### 1) One log line per level + which levels are enabled for OrderService
GET {{host}}/log

### 2) IsEnabled matrix for several categories (filter rules, most specific category wins)
GET {{host}}/levels

### 3) {UserId} template vs $"..." interpolation — what a provider really receives
GET {{host}}/structured-vs-interpolated

### 4) [LoggerMessage] source-generated logging
GET {{host}}/source-generated

### 5) BeginScope with a correlation id
GET {{host}}/scope
X-Correlation-Id: order-flow-7

### 6) LogError(ex, "...") vs interpolating the exception
GET {{host}}/exception

### 7) Leaking vs redacting secrets and PII (FAKE values)
GET {{host}}/sensitive
